ki/Black-browed_albatross","wikidataId":"Q602598"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Brown Pelican","source":"Checklist Dutch Caribbean Species Register"},{"language":"en","name":"Pelican","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Brown Pelican (Southern)","source":"The Clements Checklist"}],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Pelecanus occidentalis","confidence":99,"rank":"species","scientificName":"Pelecanus occidentalis Linnaeus, 1766","status":"ACCEPTED","usageKey":5229158},"ottId":329999,"rank":"species","scientificName":"Pelecanus occidentalis","synonyms":[],"wikipedia":{"extract":"The brown pelican (Pelecanus occidentalis) is a bird of the pelican family, Pelecanidae, one of three species found in the Americas and one of two that feed by diving into water. It is found on the Atlantic Coast from New Jersey to the mouth of the Amazon River, and along the Pacific Coast from British Columbia to Peru, including the Galapagos Islands.","revisionId":1369842920,"title":"Brown pelican","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown_pelican","wikidataId":"Q208714"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Red-winged Tinamous","source":"Catalogue of Life"}],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Rhynchotus","confidence":94,"rank":"genus","scientificName":"Rhynchotus von Spix, 1825","status":"ACCEPTED","usageKey":2477461},"ottId":402447,"rank":"genus","scientificName":"Rhynchotus","synonyms":["Rhinchotus","Rhynchotis","Rhyncotus"],"wikipedia":{"extract":"Rhynchotus is a genus of birds in the tinamou family. This genus comprises two members of this South American family.","revisionId":1341084858,"title":"Rhynchotus","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhynchotus","wikidataId":"Q1080915"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Bongolava Mouse Lemur","source":"The IUCN Red List of Threatened Species"}],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Microcebus bongolavensis","confidence":99,"rank":"species","scientificName":"Microcebus bongolavensis Olivieri, Zimmermann, Randrianambinina, Rassolohar